Paul Smee says:

}While I go for the idea of 'controlling' polypiling in some way, I
}would hate to see it eliminated.  In some games, it is the only way to
}get absolutely essential items.  If it were to be eliminated, then
}there should be some other mechanism added to the game to ensure that
}required items would be generated somewhere.

}Which leads to a more general gripe of mine, which is that there should
}be some form of 'safety latch' on randomness, to ensure that things
}which are necessary will occur/appear in sensible time.  (I.e., the
}game should always be possible to win, IF played correctly.  My
}propensity for getting myself killed is sufficiently great that I don't
}really need help in the form of impossible games.)


I agree that polypiling is needed to generate necessary items, if it is
significantly modified there needs to be some mechanism to insure that
many, if not all, items will occur *somewhere*.  I've had games turn into
endurance contests because I got to the Medusa level without a blindfold,
potion of blindness, or any of the other items that let me get past her.
My list is short, offhand some way to blind myself, some way to reflect
attacks, some way to get magic resistance, and some way to acquire a 
reasonable weapon.  But it's a waste of time to go into Hell without some
of this and going from level 2x to level 1 and back again over and over
without finding what I need isn't recreation.  The fact that I can generate
stuff to get my AC down to -47 and my level up to 30 is a byproduct, I'd
give that up as long as I get the basics.  Speaking of AC, it would seem
reasonable that if a priest increased you inherent AC past -5 you might
expect a message like "you evaporate" like when you overdue armor and weapons.

A "wand of everything" should be a wand of wishing at the same rate the
wand of wishing naturally occurs in the dungeon( 1% ? ).               


I'd be real interested in what people think is "necessary".  I'll be 
more specific if the discussion grows.



